    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504221/senior-technical-officer": {
      "title": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Launceston 1 Categories Professional Laboratory & Research Support 1 Management 1 Senior Technical Officer Apply now Job no: 504221 Work type: Full time Location: Launceston Categories: Management, Laboratory & Research Support The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Make a meaningful impact by supporting the next generation of health professionals Enjoy career development opportunities, flexible work arrangements and access to a broad range of staff benefits Full time, Fixed Term (Dec 2027) role based in Launceston About the opportunity Join the University of Tasmania's Health team as a Senior Technical Officer, where you will lead the delivery of high-quality technical and laboratory support that underpins practical learning experiences across multiple health disciplines. Reporting to the Laboratory Operations Lead, you will coordinate a team of technical staff, collaborate with academic and professional colleagues, and ensure laboratories and specialist teaching spaces are equipped, safe and ready for student learning. This is an exciting leadership opportunity for a technically skilled professional who enjoys mentoring others, driving continuous improvement, and contributing to outstanding teaching and learning outcomes in a dynamic health education environment. What you’ll do: Coordinate and provide operational oversight of technical support staff to ensure effective, efficient technical service delivery for practical teaching activities. Liaise and collaborate with a wide variety of stakeholders, both academic and professional to ensure laboratory and other ‘non classroom’ based teaching and learning activities are effectively planned and delivered. Develop capability of new and existing technical staff through agile leadership, mentoring, induction and performance planning and review. Support high quality teaching and learning experiences by providing high-level technical advice in methodologies and instrumentation. Support a safe working environment by assisting with WHS inductions, documentation, and communication of safety requirements, while proactively identifying hazards and contributing to risk mitigation activities. ­ What we’re looking for: Demonstrated ability to coordinate and oversee the work of others collaboratively, to support effective service delivery. Demonstrated ability to understand and meet internal stakeholder requirements within budget, WHS and other operating parameters, interact effectively and positively with external organisations and individuals and respond to changing needs. Demonstrated ability to analyse and solve complex technical and non-technical problems and to adapt rapidly to changing priorities and tasks. Demonstrated sound understanding and practical experience in the use maintenance and operational repair of experimental and diagnostic equipment and instrumentation. Qualifications and Licences: Current Working with Vulnerable People Registration or a willingness to obtain. UTAS Fire Warden training or willingness to obtain. Provide First Aid Qualification. Preferable: Qualification in Risk Management and Assessment. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Mandhi Allen, Laboratory Operations Lead, Mandhi.Allen@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504221 - Senior Technical Officer.pdf Applications close Tuesday, 29 September 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 14 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 29 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Senior Technical Officer Launceston 29 Sep 2026 Lead a team of technical professionals and help deliver safe, innovative and engaging laboratory experiences that support the education of future health professionals Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Senior Technical Officer Launceston 29 Sep 2026 Lead a team of technical professionals and help deliver safe, innovative and engaging laboratory experiences that support the education of future health professionals Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
